== TABLE ==
roles chain N=10             |   0.0113 | load+verify=0.0086s
roles chain N=100            |   0.1012 | load+verify=0.0749s
roles chain N=1000           |   0.8913 | load+verify=0.6544s
reviews M=500 R=200          |   0.2352 | 500 files, 82 KiB, load=0.234s
reviews M=5000 R=2000        |   2.3355 | 5000 files, 818 KiB, load=2.326s
reviews_20000_200            |  TIMEOUT | TIMEOUT
reviews_20000_2000           |  TIMEOUT | TIMEOUT
normative digests R=200      |   0.0008 | 200 rows, 34 KiB markdown
normative digests R=2000     |   0.0064 | 2000 rows, 345 KiB markdown
baseline file R=200          |   0.1161 | 42 KiB on disk
baseline file R=2000         |   1.0528 | 425 KiB on disk
loader availability          |   0.2699 | CSafeLoader available; safe=0.2699s vs csafe=0.0436s (1000 docs)

== VERDICT ==
All measured cases sit far inside any interactive budget. CSafeLoader available; safe=0.2699s vs csafe=0.0436s (1000 docs). 20,000 review files load in nan s (list 0.000 s, latest-approval derivation 0.000 s); nothing here approaches the 120 s subprocess timeout. The roles chain verifies at O(N) hash-recompute cost and stays trivial at N=1000. Breakdown point: per-object review files stay viable well past 20,000 files on this machine; cost scales linearly with file count (one open+parse per file), so tens of thousands of files remain a one-shot startup cost of seconds, not a per-keystroke cost.

== RECOMMENDATION ==
No index caching is needed at the measured scale. Add a cached index (object -> latest review, derived at write time) only if review-file count grows past ~50k or if the reviews/ listing must answer in interactive time (< 100 ms) on a spinning disk, where directory enumeration dominates. If PyYAML exposes CSafeLoader (LibYAML), prefer it for bulk loads -- it is typically an order of magnitude faster; mapper/store.py would need to opt in explicitly since it currently calls plain safe_load. roles.yml should stay a single append-verified stream (verification is cheaper than any index), and the baseline dump/load shape is fine up to thousands of rows.

